; STORE-MODEL Q13 / amendment A-6, landed with the F-26 clause in window A
; (RULINGS W3-10, adjudicated 2026-08-25): `canonS` recurses into `lit` payloads —
; one carrier, one canonical form.
;
; Two lit schemas whose object payloads differ only in key order now take the SAME
; address: the dedup L-dedup promised extends into the lit plane (F-23 closed).
; Before A-6 these were two addresses.

(schema-put (lit (obj ("alpha" (i 1)) ("beta" (s "x")))))
(schema-put (lit (obj ("beta" (s "x")) ("alpha" (i 1)))))

(assert-same @1 @2)

; One object, not two — and the store checks clean.
(check)
